    "ls|LS16_S7_U_149": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 149 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nDETECTION OF BOMB AT FARRUKHABAD RAILWAY STATION \n \n149. DR. P. VENUGOPAL:    \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is true that the timely detection of a bomb by an alert \npatrol party minutes before departure of a passenger train averted \na major tragedy in Farrukhabad railway station; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether it is also true that the Railways is r eceiving hoax calls \nregarding bomb on board of many trains in the recent past; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n       ( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n(a) to (d):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  149 BY DR. P. VENUGOPAL TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 24.02.2016 REGARDING DETECTION OF \nBOMB AT FARRUKHABAD RAILWAY STATION. \n \n(a) and (b) :  Yes, Madam. On 03.10.2015  at 06.10 hrs , one Improvised \nExplosive Device was found near parcel office of Farrukhabad Railway \nStation. The bomb was defused by the Police Bomb D isposal squad at \n13.10 hrs.  No loss of property or life was reported due to the incident. \nIn this connecti on, Government Railway Police/Farrukhabad registered \na case vide Cr. No. 36/15 u/s 03/04 of Explosive Substance Act, 1908 on \n03.10.2015. \n \n(c) and (d) : Yes, Madam. The details of hoax calls regarding bomb on \nboard trains received during the years 201 3, 201 4 and 2015  are as \nunder:-  \n \nYear Number of hoax calls received regarding  bomb on \nboard trains  \n2013 21 \n2014 34 \n2015 103 \n \n \n**** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_150": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*150 \nANSWERED ON 8TH MARCH, 2016 \n \nFOOD PROCESSING \n*150. SHRI RAJENDRA AGRAWAL: \n         Will the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the contribution of the Food Processing Sector (FPS) to the Gross \nDomestic Product (GDP) is rising over the years; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof during the last three years and the current year; \n \n(c) whether any target has been set to create employment opportuni ties in the  Food \nProcessing Sector and increase its share in GDP;  and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken to achieve the said targets? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a)  to (d):     A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *150 FOR ANSWER ON 8 TH MARCH, 2016 \nREGARDING FOOD PROCESSING \n \n(a)& (b):  As per the information provided by Central Statistics Office, Ministry of \nStatistics and Programme Implementation, the percentage share of Gross \nValue Added (GVA) from food processing in total GVA at current prices \nis as follows: \nYear Share of GVA from Food \nProcessing Industries (%) \n2011-12 1.81 \n2012-13 1.54 \n2013-14 1.44 \n2014-15 1.43 \n \n \n(c) & (d): To create employment opportunities in the food processing sector and \nincrease its share in GDP, the Ministry of Food Processing Industries is \nimplementing Schemes of Mega Food Parks, Cold Chain, Value Addition \nand Preservation Infrastructure, Setting up/ M odernization of Abattoirs \nand Strengthening of Institutions.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_151": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*151\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 8th MARCH, 2016/PHALGUNA 18, 1937 (SAKA)\nDOMESTIC VIOLENCE\n† *151. SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA:\nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of criminal cases registered in regard to domestic violence\nagainst women along with the action taken against the guilty during each\nof the last three years and the current year, State-wise;\n(b) whether women are the victims of verbal and psychological abuse in\n75 percent of cases of domestic violence and if so, the details thereof\nalong with the steps taken for appointment of protection officers to deal\nwith the said cases;\n(c) the percentage of cases of physical violence out of the cases of\ndomestic violence registered in the country during the said period;\n(d) the percentage of conviction achieved in the domestic violence cases\nregistered in the country; and\n(e) whether the conviction rate is very low due to lack of coordination\nbetween the prosecution and police and if so, the details in this regard?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\n(SHRI HARIBHAI PARATHIBHAI CHAUDHARY)\n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\n-2-\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*151\nFOR 08.03.2016.\n(a): NCRB has started collecting data under the Protection of Women\nfrom Domestic Violence Act 2005 since 2014. State/UT wise cases\nregistered, cases charge sheeted, cases convicted, persons arrested,\npersons charge sheeted and persons convicted under the Protection of\nWomen from Domestic Violence Act 2005 during 2014 is at Annexure-I.\nThe data pertaining to 2015 is being collected by NCRB.\n(b) & (c): The data on percentage of cases of physical violence out of\nDomestic Violence registered in the country is not maintained by NCRB.\nAll State Governments have appointed Protection Officers to deal with\nsuch cases as is mandated under the Protection of Women from Domestic\nViolence Act (PWDVA) 2005.\n(d) & (e): As per the information given by NCRB, the conviction rate is\n19.1% (9 cases convicted out of 47 cases in which trial is completed)\nunder PWDV Act.\n…3/\n\n-3-\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*151 FOR 8.3.2016\nAs per the seventh schedule to the Constitution of India `Police` and\n`Public Order` are State subjects and, as such, the primary responsibility\nof prevention, detection, registration, investigation and prosecution of\ncrime, lies with the State Governments/ Union Territory Administrations.\n*******\n\nPAGE 1 OF 1 OF Annexure – I\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*151 FOR 8.3.2016\nState/UT wise cases registered (CR), cases charge sheeted (CS), cases convicted (CV), cases in which trial completed (TC),\ncases conviction rate (CVR), persons arrested (PAR), persons charge sheeted (PCS) and persons convicted (PCV) under the\nProtection of Women frrom Domestic Violence Act, 2005 during 2014\nCode State/UT\n2014\nCR CS CV TC CVR PAR PCS PCV\n1 Andhra Pradesh 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n3 Assam 1 1 0 0 - 1 1 0\n4 Bihar 112 52 2 5 40.0 123 65 3\n5 Chhattisgarh 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n6 Goa 2 1 0 0 - 1 1 0\n7 Gujarat 2 2 0 1 0.0 2 2 0\n8 Haryana 4 5 0 2 0.0 3 8 0\n9 Himachal Pradesh 5 4 0 0 - 5 4 0\n10 Jammu & Kashmir 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n11 Jharkhand 5 2 0 1 0.0 4 2 0\n12 Karnataka 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n13 Kerala 140 106 2 16 12.5 116 115 2\n14 Madhya Pradesh 53 51 2 18 11.1 59 59 5\n15 Maharashtra 4 3 0 0 - 6 5 0\n16 Manipur 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n17 Meghalaya 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n18 Mizoram 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n19 Nagaland 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n20 Odisha 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n21 Punjab 2 0 0 0 - 2 0 0\n22 Rajasthan 17 11 0 0 - 16 16 0\n23 Sikkim 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n24 Tamil Nadu 4 3 0 1 0.0 4 3 0\n25 Telangana 1 1 0 0 - 3 3 0\n26 Tripura 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n27 Uttar Pradesh 66 67 2 2 100.0 345 350 2\n28 Uttarakhand 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n29 West Bengal 1 1 0 0 - 3 3 0\nTOTAL STATE(S) 419 310 8 46 17.4 693 637 12\n30 A & N Islands 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n31 Chandigarh 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n32 D&N Haveli 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n33 Daman & Diu 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n34 Delhi UT 7 2 1 1 100.0 0 2 1\n35 Lakshadweep 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\n36 Puducherry 0 0 0 0 - 0 0 0\nTOTAL UT(S) 7 2 1 1 100.0 0 2 1\nTOTAL (ALL INDIA) 426 312 9 47 19.1 693 639 13\nSource: Crime in India\nDisposal of cases/persons by police/courts may includes cases/persons of previous years also.\n******",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_152": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*152\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 8th MARCH, 2016/PHALGUNA 18, 1937 (SAKA)\nANNUAL RETURNS BY NGOS\n*152. SHRI NISHIKANT DUBEY:\nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether all the Non-Governmental Organisations (NGOs) registered\nunder the Foreign Contributions (Regulation) Act, 2010 are submitting\ntheir annual returns of accounts regularly;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) if not, the details of NGOs which have not filed their annual returns\nduring the last three years, State/UT-wise; and\n(d) the details of action taken against those defaulting NGOs under\nrelevant provisions of the law?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU)\n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\n-2-\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*152\nFOR 08.03.2016.\n(a) to (c):     As  per data maintained, out of the all associations registered\nunder Foreign  Contributions  (Regulation)  Act, 2010  (FCRA, 2010) some have\nnot filed their annual return regularly.  The State-wise/UT-wise details are at\nAnnexure.\n(d):          As per Rule 17(1) of Foreign Contribution (Regulation) Rules 2011\n(FCRR, 2011) every person who receives   foreign contribution is required to\nsubmit Annual Accounts for each financial year within a period of nine months\nfrom closure of the year  i.e.  by 31 st  December. Action against defaulter\nAssociation is initiated as per provisions contained in FCRA, 2010 and FCRR,\n2011, which include imposing of penalty , cancellation of registration etc.\nFCRA, 2010 came in to force with effect from 01/05/2011.  Since   then,\nnotices   were   issued   to around 21,000 associations in 2011 and to 10,343\nassociations in 2014 for not filing annual returns continuously for three years.\nConsequently, registration of 4138 associations was cancelled in July 2012\nand of 10,117 in March 2015 after issue of Show Cause Notices to such\nassociations and giving them adequate opportunity. In 2014, penalty\namounting to Rs.5,20,82,031/- has been imposed on 341 associations for late\nsubmission of mandatory annual returns.\n*******\n\nPAGE 1 OF 3 OF ANNEXURE\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*152 FOR 8.3.2016\nState/UT-wise details of registered associations who have not filed annual return for 2010-2011\nState\nTotal Registered\nassociations on\n31/03/2011\nTotal Number of Registered\nassociations who did not file annual\nreturn\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands 20 8\nAndhra Pradesh 5290 2561\nArunachal Pradesh 65 44\nAssam 442 186\nBihar 1772 928\nChandigarh 72 25\nChhattisgarh 305 75\nDadra & Nagar Haveli 15 4\nDaman and Diu 1 0\nDelhi 2179 716\nGoa 173 69\nGujarat 1787 637\nHaryana 241 122\nHimachal Pradesh 199 93\nJammu & Kashmir 152 58\nJharkhand 667 211\nKarnataka 2911 1270\nKerala 2786 1109\nMadhya Pradesh 839 370\nMaharashtra 3788 1682\nManipur 822 498\nMeghalaya 184 58\nMizoram 57 27\nNagaland 202 105\nOrissa 2358 1031\nPondicherry 111 31\nPunjab 220 95\nRajasthan 765 326\nSikkim 23 13\nTamil Nadu 5633 2204\nTripura 49 25\nUttar Pradesh 2932 1688\nUttarakhand 389 107\nWest Bengal 3379 1335\nTotal 40828 17711\n\nPAGE 2 OF 3 OF ANNEXURE\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*152 FOR 8.3.2016\nState/UT-wise details of registered associations who have not filed annual return for 2011-2012\nState Name\nTotal Registered\nassociations on\n31/03/2012\nTotal Number of Registered\nassociations who did not file\nannual return\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands 21 9\nAndhra Pradesh 5475 2943\nArunachal Pradesh 72 45\nAssam 457 198\nBihar 1880 1038\nChandigarh 78 27\nChhattisgarh 317 84\nDadra & Nagar Haveli 15 4\nDaman and Diu 2 1\nDelhi 2306 824\nGoa 179 94\nGujarat 1858 783\nHaryana 258 141\nHimachal Pradesh 208 96\nJammu & Kashmir 162 60\nJharkhand 710 254\nKarnataka 3075 1414\nKerala 2826 1175\nMadhya Pradesh 876 401\nMaharashtra 4045 1982\nManipur 854 569\nMeghalaya 191 57\nMizoram 66 35\nNagaland