    "ls|LS16_S7_U_159": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n DEPARTMENT OF SPACE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.159 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 24, 2016 \n \nNEW LAUNCH ORDERS \n159.  SHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD: \n Will the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether ISRO has bagged two more US launch orders; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)   whether the Antrix Corporation, ISRO's marketing arm, has \nsigned a deal with commercial weather satellite operators \nabroad; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PG & \nPENSIONS AND IN THE PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE \n(DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n(a)to(d) During October 2015, Antrix Corporation Limited (Antrix), \nthe commercial arm of Indian Space Research Organisation \n(ISRO), has s igned Launch Services Agreement with M/s. \nPlanetIQ, an American Company, for launching two of their \nsatellites on -board ISRO’s Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle \n(PSLV). These satellites are meant for studying certain \nweather parameters. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_160": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.+*160\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.03.2016\n†*160. FUNDS FOR SCHOLARSHIP SCHEMES\nSHRI LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV:\nSHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA:\nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has released the funds under various scholarship schemes\nincluding Pre -Matric and PostMatric Scholarship for Scheduled Castes (SCs) and Other\nBackward Classes (OBCs) as per the demand of the States, if not, the reasons therefor along\nwith the details of funds demanded and actually released during each of the last three years,\nState-wise;\n(b) whether funds under the said schemes have not been released by t he Government on time\nin certain cases, if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor;\n(c) whether delay in release of funds has affected the education of a large number of SC and\nOBC students and if so, the reaction of the Government thereto;\n(d) whether various States have urged the Government to release the funds for the scholarship\nschemes on time and if so, the details thereof; and\n(e) the steps taken by the Government for timely release of funds and to ensure that\nscholarship is provided to the SC and OBC students on time?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI THAAWARCHAND GEHLOT)\n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*******\n\nStatement in answer to parts (a) to (e) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 160 for\n8.03.2016 by Shri Laxmi Narayan Yadav and Shri Dushyant Chautala regarding Funds\nfor Scholarship Schemes\n(a) to (e) Government releases funds to States under the followi ng centrally sponsored\nscholarship schemes for Scheduled Caste (SC) and Other Backward Classes (BC);\n(i) Pre-Matric Scholarship to SC Students studying in classes IX and X.\n(ii) Post- Matric Scholarship to SC students\n(iii) Pre-matric Scholarship for OBC Students\n(iv) Post Matric Scholarship for OBC Students\nCentral Government releases due Central Assistance (CA) in full to the States/UTs in\nrespect of all Scholarship Schemes for SC students except Post Matric Scholarship Scheme\nfor SC students (PMS-SC). It has not been possible for the Central Government to release the\nentire due central assistance to the States/UTs with respect to PMS(SC) due to inadequate\nallocation. However, as and when funds are available CA is released without delay. The\ndetails of funds demanded and actually released during each of the last three years, State-wise\nunder PMS(SC) is attached at Annexure-I.\nThe details of fund released under Pre -matric Scholarship for SC students studying in classes\nIX and X are attached at Annexure-II.\nUnder the Scholarship Schemes for OBCs ,it is not possible for Central Government to meet\nthe full demands of the States.  Every year, the total budget provided under the schemes is\ndivided and allocated to States/UT Administrations having OBC population on notional\nallocation based on their total population (as per 2011 census data) since the State -wise\naccurate population of the OBCs is not available.  The Notional Allocation is conveyed to the\nStates/UTs at the beginning of the financial year and they are requested to send proposals\nwithin their Notional Allocation.   The States/UTs are requested to limit the number of\nscholarships to the extent of Central Assistance plus State’s Committed Liability.  However,\nthey are free to supplement their expenditu re under the schemes from the State Plan\nallocation for additional demand. The details of funds demanded and actually released during\neach of the last three years, State -wise under Post Matric and Pre -Matric Scholarship for\nOBC students are attached at Annexure-III and Annexure-IV respectively.\n*******\n\nAnnexure-I\nAnnexure referred in reply to part (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question no. 160 for 8.03.2016\nDetails of Central Assistanc