    "ls|LS16_S7_U_206": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 225 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF CITIES \nNo. 225   SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY : \n  SHRI CHANDRAKANT KHAIRE : \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state : \n(a)  Whether the Union Governm ent has details regarding \ndevelopment of cities of the country where the Union Government \nhas provided assistance under centrally sponsored scheme; \n(b) If so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor along with \nthe reaction of the Government thereto; \n(c)  The manner in which review of development work of cities is \nconducted in the absence of the said data; and \n(d) The corrective steps taken/being taken by the Government in the \nregard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO) \n \n(a)&b): The Government of India provides central assistance to \nthe States for implementing pr ojects for the de velopment of \ncities under various schemes and  as per their guidelines. The \nDetailed Project Report (DPR ) preparation and project \nimplementation etc are done by the States. The GoI keeps                          \nCont…. \n\n-2- \nrecord of funds sanctioned and re leased to the various State \nGovernments and gets regular progress reports from States. The \ndetails regarding project execution lies with State Governments. \nc)&d): The GoI reviews the progress of projects sanctioned for \nvarious States through periodi cal reports and review meeting \nwith the State Government Officials. \n \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_207": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 207 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nATOMIC POWER PLANTS WITH FOREIGN ASSISTANCE \n \n207.  SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL: \n SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has agreed to allot sit e for building nuclear power \n plants by Russian Atomic Energy Corporation and Ja pan in the country; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof including the proje ct cost and time frame set by the \n Government for completion of the project; \n \n(c)  the number of Atomic/Nuclear Power Plants esta blished in collaboration with \n Russia and Japan so far; \n \n(d)  whether the Atomic Power Plants established wi th the help of the above \n countries encountered mild impairs during its oper ationalisation; and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the measures ta ken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVAN CES & \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) The Government has already accorded in-principl e approval of the sites at \nKudankulam in Tamil Nadu and Haripur in West Bengal  for setting up nuclear \npower reactors in technical cooperation with Russia n Federation.  An \nadditional coastal site in the state of Andhra Prad esh for setting up nuclear \npower reactors with Russian technical cooperation i s also being explored.  \nThere is presently no proposal to set up nuclear po wer plants in technical \ncooperation with Japan.   \n \n \n…2/- \n \n \n\n-2- \n(b) The details of sites/projects with technical co operation with Russian \nFederation are given below:  \nLocation Nuclear Power \nProject \nCapacity \n(MW) \nSanctioned \nCost  \n(` crore) \nStatus \nKudankulam, \nTamil Nadu \nKudankulam \nNuclear Power \nProject Units \n1&2  \n(KKNPP 1&2)  \n2x1000 17270* \nKKNPP-1 is in \ncommercial operation \nsince December 2014.  \nKKNPP-2 is under \nCommissioning, \nexpected completion by \n2016-17. \nKKNPP 3&4 \n2x1000 39849 \nProject sanctioned, \nstatutory clearances \nobtained, excavation \nhas commenced.  \nKKNPP 5&6 \n2x1000 \nPre-project activities are in progress. \nStatutory clearances viz. AERB siting, \nCRZ & Environmental clearances \nobtained and Techno-Commercial \noffer under discussion. \nHaripur, \nWest Bengal Site is approved for 6 x 1000 MW (nominal). \n*under second revision to ` 22462 crore  \n(c) So far, only one nuclear power project, Kudanku lam 1&2 (2X1000 MW) has \nbeen set up in cooperation with Russian Federation. No nuclear power project \nhas been set up in cooperation with Japan. \n \n(d)&(e) The Unit-1 of Kudankulam (KKNPP-1) operated for about twenty months since \nits grid connection before it was taken for planned shutdown on June 24, 2015 \nfor refueling. The unit had generated 6875 Million Units (including infirm \ngeneration of 2243 MUs) of electricity during this period. This was the first \nplanned shutdown after a long operation and require d a detailed surveillance \nand maintenance. Thus, apart from refueling, comple ting all the surveillance \ntests as per the technical specifications, mandator y checks on various \ncomponents as per the manufacturer’s recommendation  and rectification of \nthe deficiencies identified during the inspection w ere carried out during the \nshutdown. Based on the inspections, certain design modifications and \nreplacement of a few components have also been take n up and the unit was \nsubsequently synchronised to the grid on January 30, 2016. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_209": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.209 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 11TH MARCH, 2016 \n \n \nJOINT  MILITARY  EXERCISES \n \n*209. SHRI  C. MAHENDRAN: \n SHRI  R. PARTHIPAN:  \n  \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE    j{kk ea=h     \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether India has conducted any joint military exercise with Seychelles and also \nwith Nepal; \n \n(b)  if so, the details and the outcome thereof; and \n \n(c)  the efforts being made to boost defence relations with above countries ?  \n \n                  \n   A    N    S    W    E    R \n \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                            (SHRI MANOHAR PARRIKAR) \n     j{kk ea=h                ¼Jh euksgj ijhZdj½ \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*******  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 209 FOR ANSWER ON 11.3.2016 \n \n \n(a) & (b):        Exercise ‘LAMITYE’ was conducted with Seychelles from \n15thto  28th February, 2016 with participation of 45 personnel from each side \nto enhance interoperability while carrying out counter-insurgency, counter-\nterrorism and anti -piracy operations at sea and land.  The outcomes of the \nExercise are :- \n(i) Visible professional and personal bonding between Indian \nArmy and Seychelles People’s Defence Forces personnel. \n(ii) Senior India n Army observers got an opportunity to interact \nwith the senior leadership of the Seychelles People ’s Defence \nForces and government. \n(iii) The Seychelles leadership appreciated the Indian support to the \nisland Nation and the positive momentum in Indo -Seychelles \nrelations. \nExercise ‘SURYA KIRAN’ was held between armies of India and Nepal \nfrom 09 th to 21 st February, 2016 with participation of 300 personnel \nfrom either side to enhance interoperability in jungle warfare and \ncounter-terrorism operations in mountainous  terrain and \nHumanitarian and Disaster Relief ( HADR).  The outcomes of the \nExercise are :- \n(i) Evolution of combined drills for planning and conduct of \ntactical operations in counter -terrorism environment at unit \nlevel. \n(ii) Better understanding of disaster response mechanism in \ngeneral and role of armed forces in management of disasters. \n \n(c) Apart from Joint Exercises, efforts made to boost defence \nrelations include offering training courses in Indian defence institutions, \ngifting of equipments, stores, etc .  Assi stance is also  provided to \nSeychelles in surveillance of Exclusive Economic Zone, setting up of \nCoastal Surveillance Radar Systems, Hydrography surveys, etc. \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_210": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 210\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 11TH MARCH, 2016\nHIV/AIDS\n*210. SHRI PRATHAP SIMHA:\nDR. BHOLA SINGH:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether as per an estimation of the National AIDS Control Organisation\n(NACO), approximately 2.08 million people are living with HIV in India and the\nUnited Nations (UN) has also rep orted that India has the third largest number of\npeople living with HIV in the world, if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;\n(b) whether coverage rate for HIV patients in India is only about 36 percent;\n(c) if so, the facts thereof and the reasons for this low level of coverage; and\n(d) the steps taken by the Government to increase coverage rate for HIV patients\nincluding making available the required drugs/medicines and patient care for this\ndisease?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (d):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 210* FOR 11TH MARCH, 2016\n(a)  As per India HIV estimation 2015 r eport, an estimated 21.17 lakh p eople are\nliving with HIV.\nYes, India has the third largest number of people living with HIV in the world. The\nother two countries having higher numbers are South Africa (68 lakh) and Nigeria\n(34 lakh) [Source: UNAIDS estimates 2014].\nThe details of estimated number of people living with HIV, State/UTs -wise is\nat Annexure.\n(b) & ( c) Though about 21.17 lakh people are estimated to be living with HIV\n(PLHIV), yet Antiretroviral Therapy (ART) is started only for those patients whose\nCD4 count becomes less than 350.  The total number of patients with CD4 count of\nless than 350 is estimated as 13,45,678.  Out of this, the number of people on ART is\n9.25 lakhs, making a coverage rate of 69%.\n(d) Under the National AIDS Control Programme, (NACP) Phase -IV, National\nAIDS Control Organization (NACO) provides universal access to comprehensive,\nequitable, stigma -free, quality care, support and treatment services to all People\nLiving with HIV/AIDS (PLHIV ). At present , there are 524 ART Centres and 1,094\nLink ART Centres in the country providing free Antiretroviral treatment, treatment\nfor opportunistic infections and counseling services to 9.25 lakh PLHIV. Based on\nHIV prevalence in different parts of the country, ART Centres and Link ART\nCentres are scaled up every year to match the demand. In addition, a total of 350\nCare and Support Centres (CSCs) have been established through civil society\norganizations which complement the services provided by ART cen tres through\ncounseling, outreach and linkage to need based other government welfare schemes\nand services. Constant efforts are made to increase awareness about HIV testing &\ntreatment facilities for ensuring Universal access.\nDuring the last three years, PLHIV on ART have been increasing  as follows:\nMarch, 2013 - 6,32,397;\nMarch, 2014- 7,59,242;\nMarch, 2015 -8,51,883 and\nJan,2016- 9,25,451\n….\n\nAnnexure\nEstimated Number of People living with HIV Infections (PLHIV - Adult & Children) by\nStates/UTs 2015\nStates/UT\nEstimated Number\nof People living with\nHIV Infections\nAndhra Pradesh 3,94,661\nArunachal Pradesh 606\nAssam 12,090\nBihar 1,50,689\nChhattisgarh 30,838\nDelhi 30,216\nGoa 4,619\nGujarat 1,66,333\nHimachal Pradesh 5,723\nHaryana 22,596\nJharkhand 34,386\nJammu & Kashmir 2,777\nKarnataka 1,99,060\nKerala 23,376\nMeghalaya 1,122\nMaharashtra 3,01,453\nManipur 24,457\nMadhya Pradesh 44,409\nMizoram 5,762\nNagaland 11,050\nOdisha 67,654\nPunjab 36,794\nRajasthan 1,03,148\nSikkim 939\nTamil Nadu 1,42,982\nTripura 7,238\nUttarakhand 7,059\nUttar Pradesh 1,50,361\nWest Bengal 1,28,757\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands 186\nChandigarh 2,933\nDadar& Nagar Haveli 463\nDaman & Diu 284\nPuducherry 1,560\nIndia 21,16,581",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_212": "�\n������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n��������� ������������� ��� �\n�\n����������������������������� ����������������� �\n�\n���������������������������� �\n����� � ��������������������������� �\n� ������������������ �\n� ������������������������� �\n� ���������� ���������� �\n� ���������������������������������� �\n� �������������������������� �\n� �������������������������������������������� �\n����� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ��������� ���� ��������� �����\n������� ������ ��������� ������������� ������� ���� ����� �\n���������� ��������� ����� ���� ����� ������ ��� ���� ���� ��������\n�������� �\n����� ������������������������������������������ �\n����� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ���� ��������� ��������� ��� ����\n�������������������������� �\n����� ������� ����� ����������� ������ ��� ������� ������������� ������\n������������� �������� ��� ����� ����������� ���������� ��� ���� ����\n���������������������������������������������� �\n����� ���� ����� ��� ���� ������ ���������� ��� ������ ��������� ���������\n��������������������������������� ��������������������������� �\n����� ���� �������� ��� ����� ����������������� ��������� �������� ���\n���������������������������� �\n�\n�\n\n������ �\n�����������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������� ���\n�\n���� ���������� ����������������������������������������� ���������\n���������� ���� ��������� ��� ���� ����������� ���� ����� �����������\n���������������������������� �\n���� ���������������� �\n���� ��� ������� ��� ����� ��������� ��� ����� ��� �������� ����� ����\n����������� �\n���� ��� �������� ������ ���� � �� ������ ��� ������� ������������� ������\n������������� �������� ��� ����� ����������� ���������� ��� ���������\n��������������������������������� �\n���� ��������������� ����� ������ ���������� ��� ������ ��������� ����\n������������